      "title": "insurance reserving method",
      "summary": "An insurer estimated ultimate losses from a cumulative development triangle with chain-ladder age-to-age factors. For each adjacent age, it divided the sum of later cumulative values for cohorts observed at both ages by the sum of their earlier cumulative values. It projected an immature cohort by multiplying its latest cumulative value by all remaining factors, and called projected ultimate minus latest observed the outstanding amount.",
